# List Page Shell

Use this pattern for domain **list pages** (users, services, products, spaces, tags, etc.). Defer to related rules for search ([search-input-component.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/search-input-component.mdc)), grid columns ([list-pages-card-view.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-pages-card-view.mdc)), empty state ([empty-state-component.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/empty-state-component.mdc)), and skeletons ([list-loading-skeletons.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-loading-skeletons.mdc)).

## Page root

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col min-h-0 p-4 lg:p-6 flex-1">
  <div className="flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0">
    {/* header → filters → body → pagination */}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Header row

- Title: `text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground`
- Description: `text-muted-foreground mt-1`
- Layout: `flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-6`
- Primary CTA (Add/Create) in header trailing column; use `Button variant="accent"` or outline per page pattern

## Filters toolbar

- Wrap in glass `Card` with `SearchInput` (debounce ~500ms via `onDebouncedChange`)
- **Filter** button opens advanced filters in `RightPanel` (`@/components/common/RightPanel`), not inline popovers
- Highlight active filters on the Filter button (accent border/background when any filter applied)
- Include `ViewSwitcher` (`@/components/ui/view-switcher`) when page supports grid + list

Extract filters into `<Domain>Filters.tsx` when the toolbar grows (see `UsersFilters`, `SpacesFilters`).

## Layout IDs

Add stable layout region ids on list page shells using `buildDomId` from `@/shared/utils/domId`. See [dom-element-ids.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/dom-element-ids.mdc) for the full vocabulary.

App-level debugging: `APP_LAYOUT_ID` from `domId.ts` (`#app-layout-main-content`, `#app-layout-sidebar`).

Per-page pattern (archetype: [`UsersPage.tsx`](front-end/src/features/users/pages/UsersPage/UsersPage.tsx)):

```tsx
import { buildDomId } from "@/shared/utils/domId";

const ID = {
  root: buildDomId("users", "page"),
  inner: buildDomId("users", "page-inner"),
  header: buildDomId("users", "page-header"),
  headerActions: buildDomId("users", "page-header-actions"),
  stats: buildDomId("users", "page-stats"), // when stats row exists
  body: buildDomId("users", "page-body"),
  bodyInner: buildDomId("users", "page-body-inner"),
  skeleton: buildDomId("users", "page-skeleton"),
  list: buildDomId("users", "page-list"),
  pagination: buildDomId("users", "page-pagination"),
  emptyState: buildDomId("users", "page-empty-state"),
} as const;

<div id={ID.root} className="flex flex-col min-h-0 p-4 lg:p-6 flex-1">
  <div id={ID.inner} className="flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0">
    <div id={ID.header}>...</div>
    <div id={ID.body}>...</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

- Wire `EmptyState` and `Pagination` via their `id` props where used.
- Pass `id` to `RightPanel` for filter panels (e.g. `buildDomId("users", "page-filters-panel")`).
- Skip regions the page does not have (e.g. no stats row, no pagination).

## Body states (in order)

```tsx
const showSkeleton = loading && displayedItems.length === 0;

{showSkeleton ? (
  <LoadingSkeleton viewMode={viewMode} />
) : displayedItems.length === 0 ? (
  <EmptyState icon={...} title={...} description={...} action={...} />
) : (
  <DomainList viewMode={viewMode} items={displayedItems} ... />
)}
```

- Do not show skeleton when paginating with existing rows visible
- Distinguish **empty** vs **filtered empty** in `EmptyState` description when useful

## Pagination

See [pagination-component.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/pagination-component.mdc) — `@/components/common/Pagination`, hook state, API params, and layout.

## Data hook

- Prefer a feature hook (`useUsersPage`, `useSpacesPage`, etc.) that owns search debounce, filter state, pagination, and Redux dispatch
- Keep the page component mostly orchestration + JSX

